1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Το Plex ζήτησε 120€ για να συνεχίσετε να βλέπετε από τις συσκευές σας.
Το πλήρωσα εγώ το ποσό.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Αν χρησιμοποιείτε συχνά και μπορείτε,
 οποιαδήποτε συμβολή θα εκτιμηθεί.

3
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:12,060
Who are you? Visiting hours are over.

4
00:00:13,970 --> 00:00:19,190
I am Draht, one of Aura the
Guillotine's executioners.

5
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,620
I am here to kill you.

6
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:26,180
I see. Done pretending to negotiate?

7
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:28,060
We're just getting started.

8
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:29,760
Uh-huh.

9
00:00:32,110 --> 00:00:34,580
Just so you know, I'm strong.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:37,390
Stronger than me?

11
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:40,990
Stronger than Aura the Guillotine.

12
00:00:43,670 --> 00:00:45,370
Doesn't seem like it to me.

13
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:46,880
Why not?

14
00:00:49,390 --> 00:00:51,890
This fight is already over.

15
00:00:56,230 --> 00:00:59,970
Magical wire, huh?
It's an interesting spell.

16
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:04,110
So you saved yourself from decapitation
by concentrating mana around your neck.

17
00:01:04,570 --> 00:01:05,950
You're level-headed.

18
00:01:06,510 --> 00:01:10,860
A common mage would've lost her head
without even realizing what had happened.

19
00:01:11,320 --> 00:01:15,280
But this wire is among the
strongest of demonkind's spells.

20
00:01:15,710 --> 00:01:18,730
Humanity's magic doesn't
stand a chance against it.

21
00:01:20,890 --> 00:01:24,610
I'll cut through both
your neck and your mana.

22
00:01:25,530 --> 00:01:29,620
You're right. I doubt I can
do anything about this wire.

23
00:01:31,490 --> 00:01:34,510
That's enough to convince you you've won?

24
00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:36,590
Demons these days are hopeless.

25
00:01:36,590 --> 00:01:38,710
They lack actual battle experience.

26
00:01:44,690 --> 00:01:45,850
<i>This mage...</i>

27
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:48,050
<i>She took my arm!</i>

28
00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:50,480
You bitch—

29
00:01:55,770 --> 00:01:57,260
Wait! Let's talk this—

30
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:09,070
That's one down.

31
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:20,050
<i>If I report this attack to the graf and kill
the other two, surely he'll pardon me.</i>

32
00:02:29,670 --> 00:02:31,880
The guard is dead.

33
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:36,070
<i>Like a fairy tale</i>

34
00:02:36,070 --> 00:02:38,490
<i>It's a sign the story has reached its end</i>

35
00:02:38,490 --> 00:02:41,410
<i>Like a single passage taken from</i>

36
00:02:41,410 --> 00:02:43,030
<i>A journey that was too long</i>

37
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:45,370
<i>Of the evil that once cast a shadow</i>

38
00:02:45,370 --> 00:02:47,700
<i>Across this land</i>

39
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:50,040
<i>And the memories of the short journey</i>

40
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:52,500
<i>With the hero who defeated it</i>

41
00:03:02,510 --> 00:03:04,800
<i>The story ends</i>

42
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:07,310
<i>And the hero goes to sleep</i>

43
00:03:07,310 --> 00:03:10,140
<i>Leaving this land with</i>

44
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:11,810
<i>Days of peace and quiet</i>

45
00:03:11,810 --> 00:03:14,310
<i>The passage of time heartlessly</i>

46
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:16,480
<i>Makes people forget</i>

47
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:19,280
<i>Even the tracks left behind by his life</i>

48
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:21,070
<i>Begin to rust</i>

49
00:03:21,070 --> 00:03:22,910
<i>Just the same</i>

50
00:03:22,910 --> 00:03:25,200
<i>Your words and wishes and courage</i>

51
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:28,540
<i>Are still inside of me</i>

52
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:30,410
<i>And they live on</i>

53
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:32,960
<i>We chose the same path</i>

54
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:35,080
<i>That's all it was supposed to be</i>

55
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:36,630
<i>Why is it that at some point</i>

56
00:03:36,630 --> 00:03:41,130
<i>I wanted to understand the reason for</i>

57
00:03:41,130 --> 00:03:42,260
<i>The tears that fall down my cheeks</i>

58
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:43,340
<i>Even now</i>

59
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:45,720
<i>If I retrace the journey we walked together</i>

60
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:49,260
<i>Even though you're not there</i>

61
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:50,930
<i>I know I'll be able to find it</i>

62
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:12,030
This is delicious.

63
00:04:15,020 --> 00:04:20,150
My master said any town that serves
tasty food is a good, peaceful town.

64
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:20,660
Wait!

65
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:23,350
That must be true of this town, too.

66
00:04:29,950 --> 00:04:31,190
Mr. Stark.

67
00:04:31,190 --> 00:04:32,600
You can't have any.

68
00:04:33,430 --> 00:04:37,970
Let's directly petition Graf Granat
to release Ms. Frieren.

69
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:44,620
I think it's only a matter of time
until harm comes to this town.

70
00:04:45,150 --> 00:04:49,340
We should release Ms. Frieren from the
dungeon and have her defeat the demons.

71
00:04:51,970 --> 00:04:54,120
That's our only option after all, huh?

72
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:57,070
We wouldn't stand a chance against them.

73
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:01,510
Especially not that Lügner guy.
He's unbelievably strong.

74
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:04,450
He was only looking at Frieren.

75
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:08,260
Even though we were standing there
next to him with the guards,

76
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:11,950
he was only looking at Frieren.

77
00:05:14,790 --> 00:05:17,690
It's because he thinks he
can kill us at any time.

78
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:21,210
My hands still haven't stopped shaking.

79
00:05:27,150 --> 00:05:30,480
See? I even spilled my drink
so it looks like I wet myself.

80
00:05:31,070 --> 00:05:32,910
That's just how strong he is.

81
00:05:34,060 --> 00:05:37,070
You should wipe that up. Let's go.

82
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:41,760
Lügner and his guys are with the graf.

83
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:44,510
Worst case, a fight will break out.

84
00:05:44,770 --> 00:05:47,530
That wouldn't stop the party
of heroes from going.

85
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,510
You're right.

86
00:05:53,810 --> 00:05:58,150
If I lost my nerve here, I'd never
be able to face my master again.

87
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:00,340
Let's go.

88
00:06:01,150 --> 00:06:03,020
You can keep the handkerchief.

89
00:06:03,570 --> 00:06:04,430
Huh?

90
00:06:09,390 --> 00:06:10,780
What's the matter?

91
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:13,160
I'm paralyzed with fear.

92
00:06:18,090 --> 00:06:20,750
I'm no longer detecting Draht's magic.

93
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:24,720
He must be dead.

94
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:28,750
What an idiot. He underestimated her.

95
00:06:30,060 --> 00:06:31,120
Underestimated her?

96
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:37,390
We are the right-hand men of
Lady Aura. Her executioners.

97
00:06:37,910 --> 00:06:40,510
You think we'd die from merely
underestimating someone?

98
00:06:42,530 --> 00:06:45,020
Who is that mage?

99
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:53,270
Sorry I kept you waiting.

100
00:06:55,450 --> 00:06:58,340
The mage I captured has escaped.

101
00:06:58,850 --> 00:07:01,170
The soldier guarding her cell was beheaded.

102
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:03,330
That can't be good.

103
00:07:03,330 --> 00:07:05,590
We'll help you look for her.

104
00:07:05,590 --> 00:07:07,550
Linie is skilled at locating magic—

105
00:07:07,550 --> 00:07:08,870
No, that's all right.

106
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:16,110
By the way, one of your men
seems to be missing.

107
00:07:16,990 --> 00:07:19,920
He's in the privy. He'll be back soon.

108
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:22,260
Without asking a servant for directions?

109
00:07:25,230 --> 00:07:29,160
Even I can tell she's a skilled mage.

110
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:33,240
But she allowed my guards
to seize her without a fight.

111
00:07:34,210 --> 00:07:38,010
She understands the seriousness
of killing a guard.

112
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:42,530
Lord Lügner, I'll ask you one last time.

113
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,390
Where is your man?

114
00:07:59,430 --> 00:08:01,050
Honestly.

115
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:09,920
That idiot Draht.

116
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:20,960
He ruined everything.

117
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:38,650
It's strange, though.

118
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:48,020
Now that violence has become the only way
to resolve this mess, I'm overjoyed.

119
00:08:49,750 --> 00:08:53,100
Graf Granat, what are words?

120
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:56,100
How do they differ from swords?

121
00:08:56,960 --> 00:09:00,650
No matter what we use, the weak die.

122
00:09:03,310 --> 00:09:05,870
Just like this sword's former owner.

123
00:09:06,850 --> 00:09:08,990
Lügner!

124
00:09:18,250 --> 00:09:21,430
In the end, we are wild beasts.

125
00:09:22,470 --> 00:09:25,190
Don't worry. I won't kill you.

126
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:32,110
You're going to help us remove
this town's defensive barrier.

127
00:09:37,280 --> 00:09:39,390
We should be arriving at
the graf's mansion soon.

128
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:45,180
Ms. Frieren?

129
00:09:49,040 --> 00:09:50,750
You're Ms. Frieren, aren't you?

130
00:09:58,740 --> 00:10:01,010
What are you doing here?

131
00:10:01,370 --> 00:10:03,530
Don't tell me you broke out of the dungeon.

132
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:06,580
I didn't have a choice.

133
00:10:07,310 --> 00:10:11,440
Some demon named Draht
attacked me while I was in there.

134
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:13,530
I defeated him,

135
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:17,840
but when demons die, they turn into
mana particles and disappear.

136
00:10:18,530 --> 00:10:20,510
What do you mean by that?

137
00:10:20,900 --> 00:10:24,280
He'd already killed the dungeon guard.

138
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:27,550
The only ones down there were a guard

139
00:10:27,550 --> 00:10:32,540
who had been beheaded using
magical wire and me, a mage.

140
00:10:33,330 --> 00:10:35,180
How would you read that situation?

141
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:39,520
That you're a guard-killer
who should be executed.

142
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:43,600
Right? This is becoming a pain.
I'm leaving town.

143
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,000
Wait.

144
00:10:45,470 --> 00:10:47,860
If you leave, the remaining
demons will run wild.

145
00:10:48,750 --> 00:10:51,020
Are you really going to abandon this town?

146
00:10:52,570 --> 00:10:54,640
Why don't you two defeat them?

147
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:57,270
You make it sound so easy.

148
00:10:57,750 --> 00:11:00,780
We don't stand a chance against them.

149
00:11:01,180 --> 00:11:03,900
You're not going to fight them
just because they're strong?

150
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:12,500
Besides, I don't think you're
weaker than them at all.

151
00:11:16,740 --> 00:11:18,130
Wait!

152
00:11:18,130 --> 00:11:21,890
We'll fight, okay? At least help us!

153
00:11:21,890 --> 00:11:23,140
I'm begging you!

154
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:26,630
Peek.

155
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:29,650
Hey, wait!

156
00:11:29,650 --> 00:11:31,640
Please, Frieren!

157
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:35,280
You don't know when to give up,
do you? Let's steel ourselves.

158
00:11:35,280 --> 00:11:39,160
But... it's impossible...

159
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:40,800
Don't be childish.

160
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:53,820
<i>About ten kilometers from town...</i>

161
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:55,870
<i>I sense a great deal of mana.</i>

162
00:11:55,870 --> 00:11:58,320
<i>We're being observed.</i>

163
00:12:16,230 --> 00:12:19,930
Aura the Guillotine, one of the
Seven Sages of Destruction.

164
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:25,540
I hate fighting powerful opponents, too.

165
00:12:28,790 --> 00:12:32,000
All the more reason to finish this quickly.

166
00:13:23,030 --> 00:13:26,900
Should we be sneaking
into the mansion like this?

167
00:13:27,780 --> 00:13:32,410
Would you rather tell the gate guards
that we're here to kill the peace envoys?

168
00:13:49,230 --> 00:13:50,910
It's oddly quiet.

169
00:14:00,150 --> 00:14:03,020
I love magic.

170
00:14:04,650 --> 00:14:07,390
Just as Qual, the Elder Sage of Corruption,

171
00:14:08,390 --> 00:14:14,250
spent most of his life
developing a killing spell...

172
00:14:17,460 --> 00:14:24,780
demons dedicate the entirety of our long
lives to researching a single kind of magic.

173
00:14:25,470 --> 00:14:29,340
We develop our research
daily over years and years.

174
00:14:30,090 --> 00:14:34,780
Ten years from now, our
magics will be even greater,

175
00:14:34,780 --> 00:14:37,950
and we will become even stronger.

176
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:46,310
But magic is a strange thing.

177
00:14:46,770 --> 00:14:52,370
Flamme the Legendary Mage's
defensive barrier has prevented demons

178
00:14:52,370 --> 00:14:54,720
from invading and protected this town.

179
00:15:18,980 --> 00:15:25,790
Sometimes a spell cast by a genius a thousand
years ago outmatches spells of the present.

180
00:15:28,770 --> 00:15:30,930
I despise geniuses.

181
00:15:31,380 --> 00:15:34,300
They lack the beauty of accumulated effort.

182
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:41,190
The Granat family has been entrusted with
maintaining the barrier for generations.

183
00:15:42,050 --> 00:15:49,820
If you could allow us into this town,
then there must be a way to control it.

184
00:15:50,710 --> 00:15:52,310
Teach it to me.

185
00:15:57,830 --> 00:16:00,040
I'll give you some time.

186
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:04,370
Consider it carefully.

187
00:16:05,290 --> 00:16:10,350
Making someone wait is an effective
diplomatic strategy for humans as well.

188
00:16:11,460 --> 00:16:15,650
If you won't talk, then all that
awaits you is further torture.

189
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:28,920
There must be a grimoire
related to the barrier somewhere.

190
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:32,190
Search the bedroom. I'll search the study.

191
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:49,520
You're just that adventurer kid
from this afternoon.

192
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:52,740
I thought my son had come for me.

193
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:56,150
You look awful.
Those demons did this to you?

194
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,660
I'll release you.

195
00:17:05,330 --> 00:17:06,780
You're trembling.

196
00:17:06,780 --> 00:17:08,320
Is that a problem?

197
00:17:08,320 --> 00:17:10,360
No. It's valiant.

198
00:17:11,430 --> 00:17:14,640
My dead son was trembling
before he headed off to battle, too.

199
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:22,960
Damn it. I can't cut the rope.

200
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:24,170
Is it magical?

201
00:17:24,570 --> 00:17:28,360
Don't worry about me.
I'm done for either way.

202
00:17:29,070 --> 00:17:31,910
Evacuating the townsfolk is more important.

203
00:17:31,910 --> 00:17:36,420
They're not gonna listen without you.

204
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:40,440
The Granat family crest hangs from my neck.

205
00:17:41,910 --> 00:17:45,600
Show this to the guards,
and they'll do whatever you say.

206
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:52,830
And speaking so casually to me
is a serious crime in this town, brat.

207
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:02,860
I know. Given the circumstances,
I'll overlook this offense.

208
00:18:03,620 --> 00:18:05,330
Now go.

209
00:18:05,330 --> 00:18:06,640
I see.

210
00:18:07,210 --> 00:18:08,910
Sorry, old man.

211
00:18:10,290 --> 00:18:12,650
I'm gonna break this
expensive-looking chair.

212
00:18:14,740 --> 00:18:17,000
I can't afford to replace it.

213
00:18:18,290 --> 00:18:20,560
Lord Lügner, a rat.

214
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:26,190
Graf Granat, do you know him?

215
00:18:26,190 --> 00:18:29,690
No. He's one of the adventurers
from this afternoon.

216
00:18:30,060 --> 00:18:33,380
He must've come to petition me directly

217
00:18:33,380 --> 00:18:36,070
without realizing the mage
he was with escaped.

218
00:18:37,170 --> 00:18:38,820
What a stupid kid.

219
00:18:39,410 --> 00:18:40,540
I see.

220
00:18:41,670 --> 00:18:42,830
<i>Again.</i>

221
00:18:43,290 --> 00:18:45,340
You can leave, boy.

222
00:18:45,620 --> 00:18:47,300
I'll let you live.

223
00:18:47,300 --> 00:18:48,380
<i>He's doing it again.</i>

224
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:53,170
<i>He's not even looking at me.</i>

225
00:18:54,190 --> 00:18:56,610
What's the matter? Move.

226
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:59,140
If you get in my way, I'll kill you.

227
00:19:03,050 --> 00:19:04,600
Go ahead and try!

228
00:19:08,870 --> 00:19:09,650
<i>He's fast.</i>

229
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:14,220
But you're only human.

230
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:29,590
You protected your vitals.
Your reflexes aren't bad.

231
00:19:29,590 --> 00:19:33,510
That said, the young are rash,
whether they're humans or demons—

232
00:19:33,510 --> 00:19:35,230
thoughtless and reckless.

233
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:41,640
But you challenged me alone.
I commend your valor.

234
00:19:42,250 --> 00:19:43,630
Alone?

235
00:19:43,930 --> 00:19:48,050
I see. You can't detect her after all.

236
00:19:48,050 --> 00:19:49,130
What?

237
00:19:49,460 --> 00:19:52,970
Fern, I created the opening you asked for.

238
00:19:53,740 --> 00:19:56,380
Lord Lügner, I'm sensing a mage!

239
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:12,930
<i>Impossible.</i>

240
00:20:12,930 --> 00:20:18,370
<i>A mere human mage evaded Linie's detection?</i>

241
00:20:19,750 --> 00:20:22,430
<i>And this spell...</i>

242
00:20:25,180 --> 00:20:27,840
Lord Lügner, let me handle this.

243
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:28,730
Don't.

244
00:20:29,620 --> 00:20:32,620
Girl, what is that spell?

245
00:20:33,180 --> 00:20:35,100
Ordinary offensive magic.

246
00:20:35,610 --> 00:20:40,530
I believe it's known as Zoltraak
in your magic system.

247
00:20:40,530 --> 00:20:42,910
This is Zoltraak?

248
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:45,170
Don't be absurd.

249
00:20:45,170 --> 00:20:50,080
Demonkind overcame Zoltraak
half a century ago.

250
00:20:51,150 --> 00:20:53,390
Who taught you this spell?

251
00:20:54,530 --> 00:20:56,610
You're trying to buy time, aren't you?

252
00:20:57,250 --> 00:20:58,420
I should finish you now.

253
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:00,640
I won't allow it.

254
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:03,900
Fern!

255
00:21:04,750 --> 00:21:06,920
The graf is gravely injured.

256
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:08,570
We don't have time to fight.

257
00:21:08,570 --> 00:21:09,490
Let's retreat!

258
00:21:10,690 --> 00:21:11,540
Very well.

259
00:21:21,650 --> 00:21:24,220
We'll go after them once
I've stopped my bleeding.

260
00:21:24,220 --> 00:21:26,280
You kill the warrior.

261
00:21:28,870 --> 00:21:32,280
My blood is on those two.

262
00:21:32,570 --> 00:21:34,380
We won't lose them.

263
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:38,180
You needn't fight them yourself, Lord Lügner.

264
00:21:38,410 --> 00:21:40,480
I can handle the mage as well.

265
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:44,160
If you'd been struck by that spell,
it would've killed you.

266
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:52,170
That spell has been modified
to specialize in killing demons.

267
00:21:52,750 --> 00:21:56,940
It can hardly be called Zoltraak anymore.

268
00:21:58,770 --> 00:22:01,380
It's a demon-killing spell.

269
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:05,580
The way that girl moved
reminds me of another mage.

270
00:22:06,520 --> 00:22:10,380
And I've been struck by
that same magic once before.

271
00:22:20,820 --> 00:22:22,410
I see.

272
00:22:24,130 --> 00:22:25,620
I remember now.

273
00:22:26,810 --> 00:22:28,290
It was Frieren.

274
00:22:30,090 --> 00:22:35,210
The mage who contributed significantly
to humanity's analysis of Zoltraak

275
00:22:35,210 --> 00:22:39,980
and slew more demons
than anyone else in history.

276
00:22:42,310 --> 00:22:44,500
Frieren the Slayer.

277
00:22:46,880 --> 00:22:49,570
One of the geniuses I despise.

278
00:22:49,950 --> 00:22:52,490
<i>And you alright</i>

279
00:22:52,990 --> 00:22:54,990
<i>Can you hear me</i>

280
00:22:55,790 --> 00:23:01,880
<i>Trailing along deserted train tracks</i>

281
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:04,210
<i>Crying excessively</i>

282
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:07,380
<i>Wanting you to smile</i>

283
00:23:07,380 --> 00:23:13,430
<i>I hold on to memories I'd like to keep fresh</i>

284
00:23:13,430 --> 00:23:17,140
<i>There's something I'd like to tell you</i>

285
00:23:17,140 --> 00:23:19,890
<i>With words more precious than a goodbye</i>

286
00:23:19,890 --> 00:23:25,570
<i>Unremarkable yet special</i>

287
00:23:25,570 --> 00:23:29,110
<i>See, things that couldn't have been</i>

288
00:23:29,110 --> 00:23:32,160
<i>Seen if it weren't for these eyes</i>

289
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:36,910
<i>Why? They begin to overflow</i>

290
00:23:36,910 --> 00:23:43,000
<i>So, if I were to be born again</i>

291
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:48,840
<i>I would surely choose this place once more</i>

292
00:23:48,840 --> 00:23:54,850
<i>So, if we were to meet again</i>

293
00:23:54,850 --> 00:24:00,600
<i>I'd never let you go, I'd choose the present</i>

294
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:03,560
<i>Even if no promises were made</i>

295
00:24:03,560 --> 00:24:06,480
<i>Even if I'm lost in days of loneliness</i>

296
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:12,650
<i>Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break</i>

297
00:24:12,650 --> 00:24:15,320
<i>I'm whispering our lullaby</i>

298
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:19,240
<i>for you to come back home</i>

299
00:24:20,080 --> 00:24:22,160
Lord Lügner will be upset with me again.

300
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:23,580
Seriously? This is crazy.

301
00:24:20,970 --> 00:24:23,140
You'll have to rest for a while.

302
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:24,950
You demons are monsters after all.

303
00:24:23,130 --> 00:24:25,750
Any demon can do it.

304
00:24:23,580 --> 00:24:26,980
Because I have an overwhelming advantage.

305
00:24:23,980 --> 00:24:26,600
I can kill you without mercy.

306
00:24:26,600 --> 00:24:29,960
It was Aura, one of the
Seven Sages of Destruction.
